# The curated, shareable knowledge IS committed: .lore/wiki/ (ADRs) and
# .lore/drafts/, plus .lore/config.json and .lore/hooks/.
#
# Raw evidence logs are LOCAL by design: they are large, high-churn, and would
# bloat git history forever (hundreds of MB over a project's life). They stay on
# the machine that produced them; the ADRs carry the shareable knowledge.
.lore/raw/

# Local bookkeeping that must not be shared (machine-specific cursors/locks).
.lore/meta/inference.lock
.lore/meta/previous-hooks-path.txt
